17:["$","main",null,{"id":"top","children":[["$","header",null,{"className":"border-b border-ink/10 bg-surface/40","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"mx-auto max-w-5xl px-5 py-10 sm:px-8","children":[["$","$Ld",null,{"href":"/operating-system","className":"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm font-semibold text-mute transition hover:text-accent","children":"← All chapters"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-5 flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-semibold text-accent","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"rounded-full bg-accent/12 px-2.5 py-0.5","children":"Chapter 5"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-mute","children":["· ",16," min read · illustrated"]}]]}],["$","h1",null,{"className":"mt-3 font-hand text-5xl font-bold leading-tight text-ink sm:text-6xl","children":"The Boot Process"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-lg text-mute","children":"From a cold power button to a login prompt, the whole handoff chain"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-6 flex max-w-2xl flex-col gap-3","children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"text-[1.02rem] leading-[1.75] text-ink/85","children":"When you press the power button, the machine does not magically \"have\" an operating system running. At that instant there is no kernel in memory, no scheduler, no notion of a file, just a CPU that has been given power and a small amount of code baked into a chip on the motherboard. The boot process is the carefully staged relay race that takes the computer from that bare state all the way to a login prompt, one component waking up and handing control to the next."}],["$","p","1",{"className":"text-[1.02rem] leading-[1.75] text-ink/85","children":"Each stage exists to load and start the next, slightly more capable, stage: firmware finds and runs a bootloader, the bootloader finds and runs the kernel, the kernel starts the first process, and that process brings up everything else. It is a chain of handoffs, and knowing the order matters, because when a machine \"won’t boot\", the fix depends entirely on which link in the chain failed."}],["$","p","2",{"className":"text-[1.02rem] leading-[1.75] text-ink/85","children":"This chapter follows that chain end to end. We will keep a developer’s eye on it throughout, because the boot sequence is exactly what a virtual machine reproduces, what a container deliberately skips, and what you are debugging whenever a cloud instance comes up unreachable or a service refuses to start."}]]}]]}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mx-auto flex max-w-6xl gap-10 px-5 py-12 sm:px-8","children":[["$","nav",null,{"className":"sticky top-8 hidden h-fit w-56 shrink-0 lg:block","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-3 font-hand text-xl font-bold text-ink","children":"On this page"}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"flex flex-col gap-1.5 text-sm","children":[["$","li","01-big-picture",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"#01-big-picture","className":"flex gap-2 rounded-md px-2 py-1 text-mute transition hover:bg-accent/10 hover:text-accent","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent/70","children":"01"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"leading-snug","children":"From power button to login: the big picture"}]]}]}],["$","li","02-firmware-bios-uefi",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"#02-firmware-bios-uefi","className":"flex gap-2 rounded-md px-2 py-1 text-mute transition hover:bg-accent/10 hover:text-accent","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent/70","children":"02"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"leading-snug","children":"Firmware: BIOS and UEFI"}]]}]}],["$","li","03-bootloader-grub",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"#03-bootloader-grub","className":"flex gap-2 rounded-md px-2 py-1 text-mute transition hover:bg-accent/10 hover:text-accent","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent/70","children":"03"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"leading-snug","children":"The bootloader (GRUB)"}]]}]}],"$L21","$L22","$L23","$L24"]}]]}],"$L25"]}],"$L26"]}]
